WEBVTT

00:00:08.020 --> 00:00:11.280
It's a half day tomorrow.

00:00:11.280 --> 00:00:15.280
That means I can finally go shopping in the afternoon!

00:00:15.280 --> 00:00:18.780
Or shall I take it easy at home and watch some movies?

00:00:19.150 --> 00:00:22.290
There's just so many possibilities!

00:00:27.500 --> 00:00:30.500
We have an inservice this afternoon.

00:00:35.430 --> 00:00:37.930
Shuwashuwa (Hi!) Shuwashuwa (Hi!)

00:00:35.430 --> 00:00:37.930
shuwashuwa (Hi!) shuwashuwa (Hi!)

00:00:37.930 --> 00:00:40.430
Rainbow-colored (Wow!) morning shower

00:00:37.930 --> 00:00:40.430
nanairo (Wao!) mooningu shawaa

00:00:40.430 --> 00:00:42.980
Good morning (Hi!) Good morning (Hi!)

00:00:40.430 --> 00:00:42.980
ohayou (Hi!) ohayou (Hi!)

00:00:42.980 --> 00:00:46.570
Raise your voice

00:00:42.980 --> 00:00:46.570
ookina koe dashite

00:00:50.450 --> 00:00:55.450
I liked my sketch until I woke up the next morning

00:00:50.450 --> 00:00:55.450
shitagaki manzoku hitoban tatte kara

00:00:55.450 --> 00:01:00.460
It sucks! It's terrible! I can't believe it's so bad!

00:00:55.450 --> 00:01:00.460
hetappi dameppi arienai yo

00:01:00.460 --> 00:01:05.420
Ball it up and toss it out? Change the composition?

00:01:00.460 --> 00:01:05.420
marumete suteyou ka kouzu wo kaeyou ka

00:01:05.420 --> 00:01:10.010
Confused freckles. Yaino, yaino down

00:01:05.420 --> 00:01:10.010
mayotta sobakasu yaino yaino daun

00:01:11.090 --> 00:01:16.680
A peppy Special Gold (I'm full of energy)

00:01:11.090 --> 00:01:16.680
genki na tokusei goorudo (genki desu)

00:01:16.680 --> 00:01:21.730
Add more and (Your body will) leap up during a test

00:01:16.680 --> 00:01:21.730
kasanetara (zenshin ga) tobiokiru tesuto chuu

00:01:21.730 --> 00:01:26.650
(Cut and paste, but don't mess up the layout)

00:01:21.730 --> 00:01:26.650
(kitte hatte reiauto kowasanaide)

00:01:27.320 --> 00:01:32.950
It's like a blurry photo when you frown,

00:01:27.320 --> 00:01:32.950
itsumo pinto boketa shashin mitai na

00:01:32.950 --> 00:01:37.330
So quit looking so depressed (Smile! Smile!)

00:01:32.950 --> 00:01:37.330
hekonda kao wa yosou (niko! niko!)

00:01:37.330 --> 00:01:42.830
This warm canvas has always been right here

00:01:37.330 --> 00:01:42.830
itsumo koko deshita nukumori kyanbasu

00:01:42.830 --> 00:01:47.210
Just hold on tight

00:01:42.830 --> 00:01:47.210
gyuutto dakishimete mite

00:01:47.210 --> 00:01:50.380
Three musical notes ring out

00:01:47.210 --> 00:01:50.380
oto mittsu dekita

00:01:50.380 --> 00:01:52.970
Kushakusha (Hi!) Kushakusha (Hi!)

00:01:50.380 --> 00:01:52.970
kushakusha (Hi!) kushakusha (Hi!)

00:01:52.970 --> 00:01:55.550
In the dead of the night, (Wow!) a shooting star

00:01:52.970 --> 00:01:55.550
mayonaka (Wao!) shuutingu sutaa

00:01:55.550 --> 00:01:57.970
Good night (Good!) Good night (Good!)

00:01:55.550 --> 00:01:57.970
oyasumi (Goo!) oyasumi (Goo!)

00:01:57.970 --> 00:02:01.390
I woke up when I heard you sleep talking...

00:01:57.970 --> 00:02:01.390
negoto de me ga sameta...

00:02:01.390 --> 00:02:02.390
Whew.

00:02:01.390 --> 00:02:02.390
fuu.

00:02:09.310 --> 00:02:12.320
One, two, three, four!

00:02:12.320 --> 00:02:15.320
Five, six, seven, eight!

00:02:13.740 --> 00:02:15.340
Hiro!

00:02:18.320 --> 00:02:19.740
Hello!

00:02:21.030 --> 00:02:24.330
Even if she's half asleep, just dragging her out here is progress.

00:02:26.730 --> 00:02:28.490
Something came.

00:02:28.490 --> 00:02:30.080
Some kind of flyer?

00:02:31.420 --> 00:02:33.920
Looks like they opened a diner by the station.

00:02:34.920 --> 00:02:36.880
It says they just opened today.

00:02:41.340 --> 00:02:43.100
It has coupons!

00:02:43.100 --> 00:02:46.600
Finally, a diner in our town!

00:02:46.600 --> 00:02:49.940
Hey, why don't we all go after school?

00:02:50.310 --> 00:02:51.440
That sounds great!

00:02:51.440 --> 00:02:54.760
That works out. We've got a half day.

00:02:54.760 --> 00:02:56.070
I want to go try it.

00:02:56.070 --> 00:02:58.860
Okay then, let's meet up at noon.

00:02:58.860 --> 00:03:00.070
Sure!

00:03:05.830 --> 00:03:09.210
Finally, a diner in our town!

00:03:09.210 --> 00:03:11.120
I'm looking forward to it.

00:03:11.120 --> 00:03:13.210
It has a drink bar, right?

00:03:13.210 --> 00:03:14.710
An acorn bar?

00:03:14.710 --> 00:03:17.210
No, Miya, a drink bar.

00:03:17.210 --> 00:03:20.930
You can go and have whatever you want, all-you-can-drink.

00:03:20.930 --> 00:03:23.840
All-you-can-drink!?  How much is it?

00:03:25.100 --> 00:03:27.040
About 200 yen, I think.

00:03:27.040 --> 00:03:30.480
You could probably spend all afternoon there.

00:03:31.600 --> 00:03:35.140
They've got Japanese, Chinese, and western dishes on the menu too.

00:03:35.920 --> 00:03:38.400
I used to go to one like this every once in a while at home.

00:03:38.400 --> 00:03:41.530
Were there diners where you lived?

00:03:42.930 --> 00:03:48.350
The shop I used to go to just had green tea, oolong tea, and dried food.

00:03:48.330 --> 00:03:50.790
They had free refills for ice water, though.

00:03:50.790 --> 00:03:52.540
Shop?

00:03:52.540 --> 00:03:55.880
Finally, a diner— Oh, teacher!

00:03:55.880 --> 00:03:59.380
Oh, did I interrupt your girl talk?

00:03:59.380 --> 00:04:02.470
There's a diner opening by the station today.

00:04:02.470 --> 00:04:07.330
Oh, I knew they were opening, but I didn't know it was today.

00:04:07.330 --> 00:04:11.600
You can have that one. I'll just use Miya's coupons.

00:04:11.600 --> 00:04:14.020
An economical lunchtime!

00:04:14.020 --> 00:04:15.740
Thanks!

00:04:19.400 --> 00:04:21.280
We're going in our uniforms?

00:04:21.280 --> 00:04:25.280
Yeah. It'll be more fun if it feels like we're just dropping in.

00:04:26.290 --> 00:04:27.700
I think I get what you mean.

00:04:27.700 --> 00:04:34.710
I've always wished it could be like that when we go to a café or karaoke.

00:04:34.710 --> 00:04:38.130
I guess there aren't any places near Hidamari Apartments you can stop on your way home.

00:04:38.130 --> 00:04:41.760
We can have fun like high school girls usually do.

00:04:41.760 --> 00:04:44.930
All right, let's bring our bookbags too.

00:04:46.590 --> 00:04:48.040
We're back!

00:04:48.040 --> 00:04:49.560
Welcome back!

00:04:49.560 --> 00:04:51.560
Sorry, did we make you wait?

00:04:51.560 --> 00:04:54.770
No, we just got back.

00:04:54.770 --> 00:04:56.190
Let's get going, then!

00:04:56.190 --> 00:04:58.560
Wait, don't you guys want to change?

00:05:01.110 --> 00:05:03.610
Today, we're going as high school girls!

00:05:09.860 --> 00:05:11.410
Miss Kuwahara!

00:05:11.410 --> 00:05:14.160
What's up, Miss Yoshinoya?

00:05:15.290 --> 00:05:16.920
This!

00:05:16.920 --> 00:05:19.000
Oh, it's right by the station?

00:05:19.000 --> 00:05:23.050
Yeah! School lets out early today, so why don't we go get lunch together?

00:05:23.050 --> 00:05:27.160
Really? I thought the teachers had an inservice.

00:05:27.160 --> 00:05:30.260
Isn't that why they're sending the students home early?

00:05:30.260 --> 00:05:34.390
But if we don't go by 2:00, we won't be able to use the lunch coupons!

00:05:35.000 --> 00:05:37.390
As long as we eat quick, we'll be—

00:05:41.280 --> 00:05:42.690
Miss Yoshinoya?

00:05:43.320 --> 00:05:47.450
It's nothing. I just felt like I was being watched.

00:05:47.470 --> 00:05:49.160
I must have been imagining things.

00:05:51.660 --> 00:05:56.010
It couldn't possibly work out that conveniently all the time, right?

00:05:56.860 --> 00:06:00.060
How about we just go after the inservice?

00:06:05.540 --> 00:06:08.090
Could someone be talking about me?

00:06:09.590 --> 00:06:12.810
Finally, we have a diner!

00:06:12.810 --> 00:06:15.930
It's fun going out together like this.

00:06:15.930 --> 00:06:18.480
Yeah. And we're all in our uniforms today too.

00:06:18.480 --> 00:06:22.860
It feels so novel, like we're on our way back from school.

00:06:22.860 --> 00:06:24.150
Yeah, it's fun to do this every once in a while.

00:06:25.150 --> 00:06:29.320
Nazuna, you didn't need to bring your purse with you too.

00:06:29.320 --> 00:06:31.820
Well, if we're heading back from school...

00:06:31.820 --> 00:06:35.250
Man, I'm starving! Let's run!

00:06:35.700 --> 00:06:37.200
Hold it! Miyako!

00:06:44.150 --> 00:06:45.630
It's so fresh!

00:06:46.230 --> 00:06:47.920
It did just open.

00:06:51.140 --> 00:06:52.970
Welcome!

00:06:56.140 --> 00:06:57.980
Welcome!

00:07:01.480 --> 00:07:03.520
Landlady!

00:07:03.520 --> 00:07:04.770
Hello.

00:07:04.900 --> 00:07:06.230
Hello.

00:07:06.630 --> 00:07:10.800
Hello there, and welcome to MogMog!

00:07:10.800 --> 00:07:12.490
How many will we be having today?

00:07:14.780 --> 00:07:20.540
One, two, three... Great, you're all here.

00:07:21.900 --> 00:07:23.500
You surprised me.

00:07:24.500 --> 00:07:27.550
You're working at a diner now?

00:07:27.550 --> 00:07:32.670
Yeah, I know the owner. He wanted me to help out for the opening today.

00:07:32.670 --> 00:07:34.350
Suits me pretty well, doesn't it?

00:07:34.350 --> 00:07:35.600
Yeah!

00:07:35.600 --> 00:07:38.170
Would you like the smoking section?

00:07:38.170 --> 00:07:40.240
Of course we don't!

00:07:40.240 --> 00:07:42.310
Come on, I was joking.

00:07:42.600 --> 00:07:45.400
Okay, right this way.

00:07:45.400 --> 00:07:46.650
Yay!

00:07:47.650 --> 00:07:49.650
Here's the menu.

00:07:50.690 --> 00:07:56.080
Just press the call button when you're ready to order.

00:07:56.080 --> 00:07:57.710
Okay!

00:08:00.540 --> 00:08:02.540
What should we get?

00:08:02.540 --> 00:08:05.290
They all look good.

00:08:06.540 --> 00:08:12.720
Lately, diners have been putting the Calorie
count and sodium content on the menu.

00:08:12.720 --> 00:08:16.220
Come on, don't worry about it. We hardly ever do this.

00:08:16.220 --> 00:08:18.600
It's a grand opening too.

00:08:18.600 --> 00:08:19.890
Yeah, you're right.

00:08:22.350 --> 00:08:24.230
They have macaroni gratin!

00:08:24.230 --> 00:08:26.440
That your favorite, Nazuna?

00:08:26.440 --> 00:08:29.980
Yeah, but I think I'm in the mood for pasta today.

00:08:30.630 --> 00:08:33.200
They have a lot of different kinds of pasta.

00:08:33.200 --> 00:08:34.800
Have you all decided?

00:08:34.800 --> 00:08:35.530
Yeah!

00:08:36.660 --> 00:08:38.870
All right, I'm calling her.

00:08:41.830 --> 00:08:42.970
Well...

00:08:44.190 --> 00:08:46.530
Yunocchi wanted to push it.

00:08:46.530 --> 00:08:48.440
Sorry, sorry.

00:08:52.820 --> 00:08:54.430
And what are your orders?

00:08:54.790 --> 00:08:57.390
One seafood doria.

00:08:57.390 --> 00:08:59.600
An order of salad udon.

00:09:00.210 --> 00:09:04.850
Um... A macaroni gratin, please.

00:09:05.750 --> 00:09:08.060
A Japanese-style Salisbury steak, meal A!

00:09:08.700 --> 00:09:12.050
A demiglace rice omelet, please.

00:09:12.510 --> 00:09:14.110
The MogMog steak meal!

00:09:14.110 --> 00:09:14.820
Okay, tha—

00:09:15.350 --> 00:09:17.200
And a yogurt sundae!

00:09:17.200 --> 00:09:19.490
Dessert already!

00:09:19.490 --> 00:09:21.290
What?

00:09:22.290 --> 00:09:25.540
And we'll all try the drink bar, right?

00:09:25.550 --> 00:09:26.330
Yeah!

00:09:26.330 --> 00:09:28.170
Very well.

00:09:29.460 --> 00:09:32.160
So you did end up getting the gratin.

00:09:32.160 --> 00:09:35.510
Yeah. I wasn't really sure until right when I ordered, though.

00:09:39.460 --> 00:09:41.260
Look at all the different kinds they have!

00:09:41.260 --> 00:09:43.770
I just can't decide!

00:09:44.190 --> 00:09:46.890
Nori wanted orange juice, right?

00:09:46.890 --> 00:09:47.520
Yeah.

00:09:48.520 --> 00:09:50.690
I'll get Hiro's tea.

00:09:56.900 --> 00:09:58.950
It's really packed.

00:09:58.950 --> 00:10:01.580
Well, they did just open today.

00:10:02.080 --> 00:10:04.870
There's a lot of other people in Yamabuki uniforms too.

00:10:04.870 --> 00:10:08.200
They must have all been thinking the same thing.

00:10:08.200 --> 00:10:09.920
I wonder if there's anyone we know.

00:10:10.440 --> 00:10:14.710
Someone in my class said they were going today.

00:10:14.710 --> 00:10:17.700
It's in a nice, convenient location.

00:10:17.700 --> 00:10:21.430
We can come here with friends to study before exams.

00:10:21.430 --> 00:10:24.180
And there's free refills on the drinks.

00:10:24.610 --> 00:10:29.560
Sae, you could come here when you need a change of pace.

00:10:29.560 --> 00:10:30.650
Yeah, you're right.

00:10:32.770 --> 00:10:36.190
I'm going to get another drink. What would you like, Miyako?

00:10:36.590 --> 00:10:38.320
A refill of cola!

00:10:43.190 --> 00:10:44.090
Sae!

00:10:44.090 --> 00:10:46.500
Oh, Natsume, you came too?

00:10:48.130 --> 00:10:50.710
I came with a friend!

00:10:50.710 --> 00:10:54.710
Sure. Hey, Natsume, could you grab me some sugar?

00:10:57.580 --> 00:10:58.660
How many?

00:10:58.660 --> 00:10:59.720
Two.

00:11:00.680 --> 00:11:01.780
Thanks.

00:11:01.780 --> 00:11:02.470
Creamer too, please.

00:11:08.180 --> 00:11:13.020
You have quite a sweet tooth. Isn't coffee fine with just a little milk?

00:11:14.150 --> 00:11:16.190
Someone else wanted this!

00:11:16.190 --> 00:11:17.990
This one...

00:11:19.030 --> 00:11:19.990
...is mine!

00:11:27.570 --> 00:11:28.620
Here.

00:11:34.450 --> 00:11:38.670
Sae! The cola was mine, and the coffee was supposed to be yours.

00:11:39.670 --> 00:11:43.180
Sorry. I'll get you another one.

00:11:49.810 --> 00:11:51.940
Sorry to keep you waiting!

00:11:51.940 --> 00:11:59.440
Here's your steak meal, demiglace, A meal, macaroni, salad udon, and doria!

00:12:00.650 --> 00:12:04.320
Miyako, here's some extra rice for you on the house.

00:12:04.760 --> 00:12:06.700
Thanks!

00:12:06.700 --> 00:12:08.510
Enjoy your meal.

00:12:08.510 --> 00:12:10.580
Let's eat!

00:12:10.830 --> 00:12:12.580
This is tasty!

00:12:13.120 --> 00:12:16.710
Demiglace really reminds me that I'm eating out.

00:12:17.840 --> 00:12:21.170
Yeah, rice omelets just get ketchup at home.

00:12:24.690 --> 00:12:25.740
It's tasty!

00:12:25.740 --> 00:12:28.970
Nazuna, the Salisbury steak's good too. Want to try some?

00:12:30.360 --> 00:12:32.310
You can have some of the gratin too.

00:12:36.690 --> 00:12:39.230
Slow down, Miyako.

00:12:42.730 --> 00:12:45.410
I don't understand a word you're saying.

00:12:55.130 --> 00:12:56.670
That was great!

00:12:58.040 --> 00:13:00.230
I'm stuffed!

00:13:00.230 --> 00:13:02.380
Yeah, that was satisfying.

00:13:04.720 --> 00:13:07.720
As a special for our grand opening, we're giving out ice cream samples.

00:13:11.090 --> 00:13:12.130
All right!

00:13:12.130 --> 00:13:13.930
Thanks!

00:13:15.040 --> 00:13:17.770
I shouldn't have had the yogurt sundae.

00:13:17.770 --> 00:13:21.270
You said you were stuffed, right Hiro? I'll help out!

00:13:22.280 --> 00:13:23.610
Miya!

00:13:23.610 --> 00:13:26.410
Didn't you already have a sundae?

00:13:26.410 --> 00:13:27.990
Even you, Sae?

00:13:28.420 --> 00:13:29.610
Now, now...

00:13:31.550 --> 00:13:33.270
How luxurious!

00:13:33.870 --> 00:13:35.620
I'm glad we came.

00:13:35.620 --> 00:13:36.370
Yeah!

00:13:38.380 --> 00:13:40.540
We've been here a while.

00:13:40.540 --> 00:13:42.750
Should we get going now?

00:13:43.610 --> 00:13:45.920
Had enough to drink yet, Miya?

00:13:46.400 --> 00:13:47.530
Miya?

00:13:48.330 --> 00:13:49.930
I can barely move.

00:13:56.510 --> 00:13:57.230
Miyako!

00:14:01.150 --> 00:14:05.360
Miya, you pushed yourself to try every drink, didn't you?

00:14:05.360 --> 00:14:08.160
I have a safety pin.

00:14:08.580 --> 00:14:13.480
Why don't we all have another drink while Miyako settles herself?

00:14:13.480 --> 00:14:15.000
Thanks.

00:14:16.000 --> 00:14:17.750
Come again!

00:14:21.290 --> 00:14:23.010
You look like you're pregnant.

00:14:23.010 --> 00:14:23.800
Yeah.

00:14:24.720 --> 00:14:27.630
I'm just glad I can still walk.

00:14:27.630 --> 00:14:30.550
Keep going, Miya. We're almost there.

00:14:31.890 --> 00:14:33.390
Hi, guys!

00:14:33.390 --> 00:14:36.640
Oh, Miss Yoshinoya, Miss Kuwahara!

00:14:36.640 --> 00:14:38.140
Hello!

00:14:38.560 --> 00:14:41.510
Hi. You coming back from the diner?

00:14:41.510 --> 00:14:42.390
Yeah.

00:14:42.390 --> 00:14:45.780
We're on our way there now. How was it?

00:14:45.780 --> 00:14:48.450
It was really pretty inside.

00:14:49.060 --> 00:14:51.880
The staff were on the ball.

00:14:52.680 --> 00:14:54.740
And the food was wonderful.

00:14:54.740 --> 00:14:56.040
That's great!

00:14:57.040 --> 00:14:58.910
Sorry, I beat you to it.

00:14:58.910 --> 00:15:01.670
Miyako beat me to it!?

00:15:02.250 --> 00:15:03.670
She just had too much to drink.

00:15:06.760 --> 00:15:08.760
All right!

00:15:09.200 --> 00:15:12.550
Nori, can we go over our homework later?

00:15:12.550 --> 00:15:14.910
Sure, let's study together.

00:15:14.910 --> 00:15:16.970
Miya, take care of yourself, okay?

00:15:16.970 --> 00:15:20.850
I'm fine now. Thanks for the safety pin, Hiro.

00:15:22.810 --> 00:15:25.330
Thanks for having me along today.

00:15:25.330 --> 00:15:27.270
See you, Nazuna.

00:15:27.270 --> 00:15:28.120
Yeah.

00:15:31.860 --> 00:15:36.950
I'm so disappointed. Yunocchi, sorry for not living up to expectations.

00:15:37.990 --> 00:15:43.080
I actually missed two different drinks.

00:15:43.080 --> 00:15:45.250
I couldn't try them all.

00:15:45.690 --> 00:15:47.250
We can always go again.

00:15:47.250 --> 00:15:48.300
Yeah!

00:15:49.880 --> 00:15:50.640
Later!

00:16:02.950 --> 00:16:05.770
I guess Miya's back to herself.

00:16:05.770 --> 00:16:12.780
Finally, a diner in our town!

00:16:18.790 --> 00:16:19.790
One!

00:16:21.830 --> 00:16:23.920
Mom, you can't come to my entrance ceremony?

00:16:23.920 --> 00:16:28.170
That's right. I'm sorry, but something suddenly came up at work.

00:16:30.420 --> 00:16:32.920
I really wanted to go, but...

00:16:35.500 --> 00:16:38.680
Then I'm going by myself?

00:16:54.650 --> 00:16:56.780
Ten minutes from home by bike...

00:16:58.040 --> 00:16:59.790
Then I get on the train...

00:17:03.830 --> 00:17:05.960
...which rattles its way along for forty-two minutes.

00:17:07.370 --> 00:17:08.750
It's so far.

00:17:09.300 --> 00:17:13.210
This far away, none of my friends from middle school will be there.

00:17:14.010 --> 00:17:17.590
I was really looking forward to the entrance ceremony,

00:17:17.590 --> 00:17:19.890
but it's so disheartening going alone.

00:17:23.390 --> 00:17:25.390
Apologies for the inconvenience.

00:17:25.850 --> 00:17:29.900
Due to signaling problems, we have been forced to make an emergency stop.

00:17:30.970 --> 00:17:35.400
There will be a short delay while we test the system.

00:17:35.400 --> 00:17:36.910
No way!

00:17:50.080 --> 00:17:53.670
Why is this happening to me on the day of the entrance ceremony!?

00:17:54.810 --> 00:17:58.180
I don't even see anyone in a Yamabuki uniform!

00:18:00.630 --> 00:18:02.180
I'm going the wrong way!

00:18:05.490 --> 00:18:07.270
But I'm not gonna cry.

00:18:07.270 --> 00:18:08.890
I won't cry!

00:18:15.090 --> 00:18:16.560
I finally made it.

00:18:20.910 --> 00:18:23.540
Let's see, Natsume, Natsume...

00:18:24.060 --> 00:18:25.290
B-18!

00:18:31.610 --> 00:18:36.840
But why? This is number 18, isn't it?

00:18:41.030 --> 00:18:43.760
Why has everything been going wrong?

00:18:45.850 --> 00:18:50.350
This is my one entrance ceremony. I was looking forward to it so much.

00:18:50.900 --> 00:18:53.730
But I don't know if I can take it alone.

00:18:53.770 --> 00:18:56.110
Are you sure you've got the right class?

00:18:58.860 --> 00:19:01.240
Those are for the art department's class A.

00:19:02.490 --> 00:19:04.370
Are you looking for another class?

00:19:07.980 --> 00:19:10.620
Class A... I had the wrong one.

00:19:10.620 --> 00:19:12.380
Class B is over here.

00:19:13.380 --> 00:19:14.880
We'd better hurry.

00:19:17.470 --> 00:19:18.640
Thanks.

00:19:21.560 --> 00:19:23.260
Was your train late too?

00:19:24.470 --> 00:19:29.560
Train? No, I live in front of the school.

00:19:29.580 --> 00:19:32.520
The award deadline is tomorrow, so I was up late last night.

00:19:34.020 --> 00:19:35.220
Award?

00:19:35.220 --> 00:19:38.650
Yeah, for fiction. Writing is my hobby.

00:19:39.050 --> 00:19:40.900
I've been working so hard on it...

00:19:43.410 --> 00:19:47.040
...I haven't even had the chance to say hi to the other people in my building.

00:19:49.040 --> 00:19:51.540
Oh, there's the line! Looks like we made it.

00:19:51.940 --> 00:19:54.540
Sorry to just blab at you like that.

00:19:56.290 --> 00:19:56.800
I'm...

00:19:57.800 --> 00:19:59.310
I'm Natsume!

00:19:59.800 --> 00:20:00.800
What's your name?

00:20:06.220 --> 00:20:07.520
Sae.

00:20:10.820 --> 00:20:12.560
I guess she lives alone.

00:20:12.990 --> 00:20:15.240
She's in the art program, but she writes...

00:20:15.240 --> 00:20:16.560
She's tall...

00:20:18.310 --> 00:20:20.370
There's so much I want to talk to her about.

00:20:21.200 --> 00:20:22.820
I wonder if we'll get along.

00:20:23.430 --> 00:20:26.320
Maybe we can become close friends.

00:20:26.320 --> 00:20:29.330
Or so Natsume thought, but...

00:20:29.330 --> 00:20:35.210
At the welcoming party, physicals, orientation, and on and on...

00:20:35.210 --> 00:20:39.710
With each event split by class, misfortune kept the two separated,

00:20:40.200 --> 00:20:43.760
unable to speak, and thus ten days passed.

00:20:46.170 --> 00:20:49.340
Hey, class A is in homeroom now, right?

00:20:49.340 --> 00:20:51.520
Yeah, I think so.

00:20:53.890 --> 00:20:56.100
I wonder if Sae's there.

00:20:56.100 --> 00:20:58.520
I have a lot of friends in my class now.

00:20:59.220 --> 00:21:01.530
I was a little shy then, but...

00:21:03.230 --> 00:21:05.670
Now I have plenty to talk about!

00:21:08.160 --> 00:21:09.160
There she is!

00:21:12.800 --> 00:21:13.120
Sa—

00:21:13.120 --> 00:21:13.790
Sae!

00:21:14.420 --> 00:21:19.410
I was thinking of making stew tonight. Would you like some?

00:21:19.410 --> 00:21:22.300
Thanks! I'll go shopping with you, then.

00:21:24.190 --> 00:21:27.300
What's this casual conversation? Who's that cute girl!?

00:21:27.720 --> 00:21:31.180
Are they in the same class and the same apartment building?

00:21:31.190 --> 00:21:32.680
No way...

00:21:32.680 --> 00:21:33.990
Oh, Natsume!

00:21:33.990 --> 00:21:35.690
It's been a while. How have you—

00:21:35.690 --> 00:21:38.440
Sorry, I'm very busy right now!

00:21:39.520 --> 00:21:41.770
I don't have time to chat like you do!

00:21:53.790 --> 00:21:55.250
Sae, you idiot!

00:21:55.830 --> 00:21:59.790
But she didn't really do anything wrong. I'm terrible.

00:22:00.920 --> 00:22:04.210
But she didn't even pay attention to how I felt!

00:22:11.470 --> 00:22:16.940
I first met you on a fresh new spring day

00:22:11.470 --> 00:22:16.940
atarashii haru no hi kimi to deatta

00:22:16.560 --> 00:22:21.310
A flower blossomed in my heart, a flower in full bloom

00:22:16.560 --> 00:22:21.310
kokoro ni hana ga saku mankai no hana

00:22:21.310 --> 00:22:29.490
I can see cherry blossoms from my window

00:22:21.310 --> 00:22:29.490
sakura ga mieru yo mado kara

00:22:32.330 --> 00:22:37.290
Another spring went by, but my feelings haven't changed

00:22:32.330 --> 00:22:37.290
nidome no haru ga sugi kawaranai omoi

00:22:37.370 --> 00:22:42.000
I'll try to close the distance lingering between us

00:22:37.370 --> 00:22:42.000
chijimanakatta kyori arukidashite miyou

00:22:42.170 --> 00:22:47.800
I waited for you along the path you take home,

00:22:42.170 --> 00:22:47.800
guuzen wo yosootte kimi wo

00:22:47.800 --> 00:22:51.800
But I pretended it was just a coincidence

00:22:47.800 --> 00:22:51.800
kaeri michi machibuse shita

00:22:52.640 --> 00:22:57.600
The flower petals in my palm swayed in the breeze

00:22:52.640 --> 00:22:57.600
te no hira ni hanabira hirari

00:22:57.730 --> 00:23:04.770
Your smile and the scenery are seared into my eyes

00:22:57.730 --> 00:23:04.770
kimi no egao me ni yakitsuketa keshiki

00:23:04.770 --> 00:23:10.200
The cherry blossoms are flowering, and I want to see you

00:23:04.770 --> 00:23:10.200
sakura saku kimi ni aitai

00:23:10.200 --> 00:23:15.080
If only I could always be with you

00:23:10.200 --> 00:23:15.080
kimi to zutto ireta nara

00:23:15.080 --> 00:23:21.210
So many cherry blossoms are flowering

00:23:15.080 --> 00:23:21.210
sakura sakura saiteru suki dayo

00:23:21.210 --> 00:23:31.010
I can feel this shining season in my heart, and I love it

00:23:21.210 --> 00:23:31.010
koko ni aru kagayaita kisetsu wo

00:23:40.610 --> 00:23:42.610
Let's try to sum up Hidamari Apartments in one phrase!

00:23:42.610 --> 00:23:44.400
Um... Hidamaria.

00:23:44.400 --> 00:23:46.460
A sunny place with a zero-minute commute!

00:23:46.460 --> 00:23:48.610
Come on, we're not trying to write a real estate ad here.

00:23:48.610 --> 00:23:51.850
How about "Hidamari Apartments, a calming place for girls"?

00:23:51.850 --> 00:23:53.040
That sounds wonderful.

00:23:53.040 --> 00:23:57.240
Are you talking about songs? Yamabuki number one!

00:23:57.260 --> 00:23:59.140
Not quite, teacher.

00:23:59.140 --> 00:24:05.710
Next time, "June 23rd~25th: I'm Home" and "July 30th: Barbecue."

00:24:05.710 --> 00:24:09.660
We'll be waiting at Hidamari Apartments. Be sure to come see us!
